From 9c62b4b74ccdc01a0fdf9e01c050d5a30466e222 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 09:34:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] TileLang rank-order reduce-scatter

A reduce-scatter with sparknet's one-shot all-reduce arithmetic: the chunks
are exchanged unreduced over the group's NCCL communicator (the same bytes)
and added in FP32 in rank order, rounded once, by a TileLang kernel that
reads this rank's chunk in place. NCCL's reduce-scatter adds around the ring
from the owner's neighbour and rounds every hop, so under prefill sequence
parallelism a row's bits depend on the step's row count; this does not.

At four ranks only ring neighbours exchange: the opposite rank's chunk is
relayed in halves, one through each neighbour, as on ring4 where opposite
ranks are not cabled. Nothing calls it yet.
